{"schemaVersion":1,"systemCode":"BGN-PCGN:kbd-Cyrl:Latn:2011","dependencies":[],"metadata":{"authority_id":"bgnpcgn","id":"2011","language":"iso-639-2:kbd","source_script":"Cyrl","destination_script":"Latn","name":"Romanization of Kabardian (2011)","url":"https://www.gov.uk/government/organisations/permanent-committee-on-geographical-names","creation_date":"2011","confirmation_date":"2017-10","description":"The BGN/PCGN system for Kabardian is designed for use in romanizing names written in the\n    Kabardian Cyrillic alphabet. Kabardian, of the north-western Caucasian language family, is\n    principally spoken in Russia's republics of Kabardino-Balkariya and Karachayevo-Cherkesiya\n    and has been written in a modified Cyrillic script since 1936. Also known as East\n    Circassian, Kabardian is notable for its rich density of consonant phonemes (most\n    commentators agree on an inventory of 47 or 48) and corresponding paucity of vowels.\n    Kabardian letters are addressed in the romanizations as per their articulation:\n    glottalised consonants are marked with an apostrophe, and labialized consonants with w.","notes":["У should be romanized as w or u according to context: w should be used word-initially, and u used elsewhere, except as in combinations occurring elsewhere in the table.","The characters Ё, Ъ, Ы and Ь (except as they occur in character combinations addressed elsewhere in the table) appear only in Russian loan words, and are thus romanized in the same style as in the BGN/PCGN Romanization System for Russian.","The letter Хь is romanized h with the combining macron below (U+0048+0033 for the capital; U+1E96 precomposed for the lower case); the table column shows the precomposed ẖ.","An inventory of letter-diacritic combinations, with their Unicode encoding, in addition to the unmodified letters of the basic Roman script is:","All apostrophes appearing in romanization are U+2019","Ä (U+00C4)  ä (U+00E4)  Ź (U+0179)  ź (U+017A)  Ś (U+015A)  ś (U+015B)  Ë (U+00CB)  ë (U+00EB)  H̱ (0048+0031)  ẖ (0068+0031)","The source document prints the H̱ inventory codepoint as 0048+0031; the glyph shown is h with the combining macron below (U+0331).","The Romanization columns show only lowercase forms but, when romanizing, uppercase and lowercase Roman letters as appropriate should be used."]},"stages":[{"kind":"stage","name":"main","rules":[{"kind":"sub","from":{"kind":"group","items":[{"kind":"alias","name":"boundary"},{"kind":"string","value":"У"}]},"to":{"kind":"string","value":"W"}},{"kind":"sub","from":{"kind":"group","items":[{"kind":"alias","name":"boundary"},{"kind":"string","value":"у"}]},"to":{"kind":"string","value":"w"}},{"kind":"parallel","rules":[{"kind":"sub","from":{"kind":"string","value":"Кхъу"},"to":{"kind":"string","value":"Qw"}},{"kind":"sub","from":{"kind":"string","value":"Гъу"},"to":{"kind":"string","value":"Ghw"}},{"kind":"sub","from":{"kind":"string","value":"Къу"},"to":{"kind":"string","value":"Qw’"}},{"kind":"sub","from":{"kind":"string","value":"КӀу"},"to":{"kind":"string","value":"Kw’"}},{"kind":"sub","from":{"kind":"string","value":"Хъу"},"to":{"kind":"string","value":"Xw"}},{"kind":"sub","from":{"kind":"string","value":"Кхъ"},"to":{"kind":"string","value":"Q"}},{"kind":"sub","from":{"kind":"string","value":"Гу"},"to":{"kind":"string","value":"Gw"}},{"kind":"sub","from":{"kind":"string","value":"Гъ"},"to":{"kind":"string","value":"Gh"}},{"kind":"sub","from":{"kind":"string","value":"Дж"},"to":{"kind":"string","value":"J"}},{"kind":"sub","from":{"kind":"string","value":"Дз"},"to":{"kind":"string","value":"Dz"}},{"kind":"sub","from":{"kind":"string","value":"Жь"},"to":{"kind":"string","value":"Ź"}},{"kind":"sub","from":{"kind":"string","value":"Ку"},"to":{"kind":"string","value":"Kw"}},{"kind":"sub","from":{"kind":"string","value":"КӀ"},"to":{"kind":"string","value":"K’"}},{"kind":"sub","from":{"kind":"string","value":"Къ"},"to":{"kind":"string","value":"Q’"}},{"kind":"sub","from":{"kind":"st